<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#09130d" />
    <title>Eshyra - A text-first, persistent AI Dungeon Master</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Eshyra is a campaign engine for long-running fantasy play: it remembers prior events, tracks structured game state, adjudicates rules through deterministic tools, and sustains a tabletop-like solo or small-group experience entirely through text. Download the openly licensed D&D 5e SRD 5.1 rules pack."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://eshyra.app/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://eshyra.app/" />
    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="Eshyra - A text-first, persistent AI Dungeon Master"
    />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="A text-first campaign engine for long-running fantasy play, plus an openly licensed D&D 5e SRD 5.1 rules pack you can download today."
    />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://eshyra.app/art/backdrop-mural.png" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
    {{SITE_ICONS}}
  </head>
  <body>
    {{SITE_HEADER}}
    <main class="page-shell" id="main">
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">A WORLD WORTH REMEMBERING</p>
          <h1 id="intro-title">ESHYRA</h1>
          <p class="hero-deck">A text-first, persistent<br />AI Dungeon Master.</p>
          <p class="hero-description">Long-running fantasy campaigns.<br />A world that remembers.<br />A story shaped by you.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="#essays">Explore the essays <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a>
          <p class="project-status">Early pre-release</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-art">
          <img src="/art/midnight-library.webp" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" alt="A blue-robed wizard at an amber computer terminal in a candlelit library overlooking a moonlit fantasy city" />
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section class="essays-section" id="essays" aria-labelledby="essays-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="essays-title">Essays</h2><a href="/essays/">All essays &rarr;</a></div>
        <p class="section-intro">Lessons learned building Eshyra: agentic software engineering, persistent worlds, and the decisions behind the project.</p>
        {{ESSAY_CARDS}}
      </section>
      <section class="about-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="about-title">The project</h2><span>IN DEVELOPMENT</span></div>
        <div class="about-columns">
          <p>Eshyra is a campaign engine for long-running fantasy play: it remembers prior events, tracks structured game state, adjudicates rules through deterministic tools, and sustains a tabletop-like solo or small-group experience entirely through text.</p>
          <div><p>Eshyra itself is early pre-release and under construction. There is no sign-up yet. In the meantime, the project has produced something useful on its own: a structured, openly licensed D&amp;D 5e SRD rules pack you can download and use today.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/jbongaarts/eshyra">Follow development on GitHub &nearr;</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section
        class="resource-panel"
        id="rules-pack"
        aria-labelledby="rules-pack-title"
      >

        <div class="terminal-body">
          <div class="resource-intro">
            <div>
              <h2 id="rules-pack-title">D&amp;D 5e SRD 5.1 rules pack</h2>
              <p class="lede">
                A structured, machine-friendly representation of the
                <strong>System Reference Document 5.1</strong>, extracted by
                Eshyra's deterministic importer into a single JSON records file
                with per-record provenance. Useful for tools, bots, search
                indexes, and other tabletop software.
              </p>

              <p class="story-link">
                <span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
                <a href="/rules-pack/"
                  >How and why this rules pack is built</a
                >
                &mdash; the engineering story behind the pack: a
                source-grounded rules compiler, executable curation, and the
                boundary between an AI Dungeon Master and a deterministic rules
                engine.
              </p>

              <p class="callout">
                This is reference data derived from CC BY 4.0 source material.
                It is <strong>not</strong> original game content and
                <strong>not</strong> an endorsement by Wizards of the Coast.
              </p>
            </div>


          </div>

          <dl class="stats" aria-label="Rules-pack statistics">
            <div>
              <dt>records</dt>
              <dd>{{RECORD_COUNT}}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>record kinds</dt>
              <dd>{{KIND_COUNT}}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>pack size</dt>
              <dd>{{ZIP_SIZE}}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <a class="download-button" href="/downloads/{{ZIP_NAME}}" download>
            <span aria-hidden="true">[ &darr; ]</span>
            Download rules pack ({{ZIP_SIZE}})
          </a>

          <dl class="metadata">
            <div>
              <dt>LICENSE:</dt>
              <dd>Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>SOURCE:</dt>
              <dd>SRD 5.1 ({{SOURCE_DATE}})</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>BUILT:</dt>
              <dd>{{BUILD_DATE}}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <details class="provenance">
            <summary>
              <span aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
              What's inside &amp; how to verify it
            </summary>
            <div>
              <p>
                The ZIP contains <code>manifest.json</code>,
                <code>records.json</code>, <code>ATTRIBUTION.txt</code>, and a
                short <code>README.md</code>. Each record names the SRD location
                it was extracted from.
              </p>
              <p class="hashes">
                ZIP SHA-256:
                <code>{{ZIP_SHA256}}</code><br />
                Source SRD 5.1 SHA-256:
                <code>{{SOURCE_HASH}}</code>
              </p>
              <table class="kinds">
                <caption>
                  Record kind counts
                </caption>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Record kind</th>
                    <th scope="col">Count</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
{{KINDS_ROWS}}
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <p>
                Prefer the source? Browse and diff the rules-pack files directly
                in the repository:
                <a
                  href="https://github.com/jbongaarts/eshyra/tree/main/packages/core/data/rules-packs/rules__dnd5e-srd-5.1"
                  >github.com/jbongaarts/eshyra</a
                >.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="resource-panel" id="license" aria-labelledby="license-title">

        <div class="terminal-body">
          <div class="resource-intro">


            <div>
              <h2 id="license-title">License &amp; attribution</h2>
              <p class="lede">
                The rules pack is distributed under the
                <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"
                  >Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License</a
                >. If you redistribute these records or derivatives, preserve
                the attribution below.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <blockquote class="attribution">
            This work includes material taken from the System Reference Document
            5.1 (&ldquo;SRD 5.1&rdquo;) by Wizards of the Coast LLC and available
            at
            <a href="https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document"
              >dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document</a
            >. The SRD 5.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution
            4.0 International License available at
            <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"
              >creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode</a
            >.
          </blockquote>
          <p class="lede">
            The Eshyra application itself is a separate work and is not offered
            here; its source is governed by its own license in the
            <a href="https://github.com/jbongaarts/eshyra">repository</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
    {{SITE_FOOTER}}
  </body>
</html>
